# Ruby ships json as a DEFAULT gem; the toolchain image's ruby (4.0.6) bundles
# json 2.18.0 under /mise/installs/ruby. The app does NOT load it — it runs the
# patched vendored copy pinned in backend/Gemfile.lock (json 2.21.1) under
# BUNDLE_DEPLOYMENT. The default gemspec is a dormant file, but the scanner
# still flags it. Remove once the ruby toolchain ships a fixed default.
# Tracked in #485.
CVE-2026-33210

# Same shape for resolv: ruby 4.0.6's default gem is 0.7.0, the fixed release is
# 0.7.2 (vendored via backend/Gemfile.lock, so that's what any require gets).
# The default gemspec stays on disk and the scanner keeps flagging it.
CVE-2026-80212
